  "notes": "The library’s tour and level guide describe five library levels, the covered open-air Knowledge Walk and floating balcony, shaded river decks, an external red reading room with two levels of glazing, and Stanley Place exterior blades. The state conservation plan and design team describe recessed river glazing, cubic concrete masses, terraces and overhangs."
